    "body": "Two things occur to me about this. One is that often the operating system doesn't even know the physical size, so the returned values from such an API still ultimately need to be taken with a grain of salt by authors; Windows often falls back to just guessing that a 1080 display is 96DPI. The other is that it could raise fingerprinting concerns, since monitor physical sizes have more variation than monitor pixel counts.",
